<title>KUWAIT: Kuwait bank assets rise in November month/month.</title>
<headline>Kuwait bank assets rise in November month/month.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Combined assets of banks operating in Kuwait rose to 11.423 billion dinars at the end of November from 11.348 billion at the end of October, Central Bank said in a monthly bulletin.</p>
<p>Assets were 11.657 billion dinars in November 1995.</p>
<p>			Figures in million Kuwaiti dinars</p>
<p>					    November '96    November '95</p>
<p> Cash					  46.8		 50.3</p>
<p> Balances with Central Bank	    44.5		 32.9</p>
<p> Public debt instruments	    1,699.5	    1,957.7</p>
<p> Debt purchase bonds		  2,883.6	    3,644.4</p>
<p> Other local investments		297.4		343.4</p>
<p>Credit facilities to</p>
<p>  residents			     3,198.7	    2,247.0</p>
<p> Foreign assets			 2,153.4	    2,226.8</p>
<p> Inter bank local deposits	    602.8		659.9</p>
<p> Other assets			     496.5		494.0</p>
<p> Total				   11,423.2	   11,656.5</p>
<p>Note: Data covers eight commercial and specialised banks, the Islamic institution Kuwait Finance House and a Kuwaiti branch of a Bahrain-based bank.</p>
<p>Debt purchase bonds include the value of the purchase by the government of the real estate portfolio of Kuwait Finance House in December 1991.</p>
<p>Slight discrepancies in totals are due to rounding.</p>
<p>($1 = 0.303 dinar)</p>
</text>
